WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.300
Two GPS questions hide inside "does this reaction work?"

2
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.920
First: will this route actually reach the destination?

3
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:16.880
That is thermodynamics, ΔG, and it tells you whether the reaction is favorable

4
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.780
at all. Second: how congested is the road?

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.500
That is kinetics, ΔG‡, the activation energy, and it tells you

6
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.740
how fast you'll get there.

7
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.540
Here's the line to remember: an enzyme answers only the second question.

8
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.440
It never changes whether a reaction can happen, only how fast.

9
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.093
Map the sign of ΔG onto a traffic light.

10
00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:45.213
Green ΔG less than zero means go: the reaction is spontaneous.

11
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:50.353
Yellow ΔG equals zero is equilibrium, no net movement.

12
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:56.073
Red ΔG greater than zero means stop: the cell has to spend energy to push it

13
00:00:56.073 --> 00:01:01.073
forward. The crucial part is the caption: an enzyme cannot change the color of the

14
00:01:01.073 --> 00:01:04.193
light. It can only speed your passage through a green one.

15
00:01:04.193 --> 00:01:08.513
Spontaneity belongs to thermodynamics, not the catalyst.

16
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.967
A picture for the next section.

17
00:01:11.407 --> 00:01:15.827
Without an enzyme, reactants have to climb over a high mountain, the long way around.

18
00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:19.287
With an enzyme, they take a shortcut through a lower pass.

19
00:01:19.907 --> 00:01:24.227
Notice both routes end at the same place on the far side: the enzyme doesn't move

20
00:01:24.227 --> 00:01:27.007
the destination, it just makes the crossing easier.

21
00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:29.667
So how exactly does it lower the pass?

22
00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:33.127
That is the transition state secret, coming up.

23
00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:37.167
This is the single most important diagram in the chapter.

24
00:01:37.707 --> 00:01:43.607
Both curves start at the same substrate and end at the same product, so ΔG, the

25
00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:48.367
overall free energy change, is identical with or without the enzyme.

26
00:01:49.087 --> 00:01:54.607
What changes is the height of the hill in between: the activation energy, ΔG‡,

27
00:01:54.607 --> 00:01:58.087
double dagger, is far lower when the enzyme is present.

28
00:01:58.847 --> 00:02:03.607
Enzymes speed reactions by stabilizing the transition state at the top of that hill,

29
00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:06.307
not by changing where the reaction ends up.

30
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.070
The transition state is neither substrate nor product: it's a fleeting, highest

31
00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.070
energy arrangement of atoms that exists for about 10 femtoseconds.

32
00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:19.930
The top row shows the arc: substrate in, transition state, product out.

33
00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.930
The bottom row zooms in on the chemistry: bonds half broken and half formed at the

34
00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:30.450
same instant. The key insight: that transition state has a specific geometry, and

35
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.190
it's the shape evolution has tuned the enzyme to recognize and grip.

36
00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.933
Four panels, one idea.

37
00:02:37.953 --> 00:02:42.173
First, the enzyme lowers the activation barrier by releasing binding energy right at

38
00:02:42.173 --> 00:02:43.213
the transition state.

39
00:02:44.073 --> 00:02:49.293
Second, shape complementarity: the active site fits the transition state better than

40
00:02:49.293 --> 00:02:50.833
it fits the ground state substrate.

41
00:02:51.613 --> 00:02:57.293
Third, the bookkeeping: catalyzed ΔG‡ equals the uncatalyzed

42
00:02:57.293 --> 00:02:59.673
barrier minus the binding energy.

43
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:05.733
Fourth, the payoff in medicine: drugs shaped like the transition state exploit that

44
00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:09.273
tight fit, binding far harder than substrate mimics.

45
00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:14.813
The enzyme's job, in one line: bind the transition state tighter than the substrate.
